  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1044 PM CDT Sat Jul 25 2026\n\nThe rather mundane forecast will persist Monday through the end of \nthe week. The large upper high pressure dominating the region will \nslowly shift westward but remain the significant influence over the \nregion, bringing essentially no change to the hot and dry conditions \nwe have seen as of late. Highs Monday will again increase a degree \nor two and remain steady thereafter. Highs on the Caprock are \nexpected in the low 100s, while highs around 105 off the Caprock may \nprompt several days worth of Heat Advisories. The next chance of any \nprecipitation will not occur until late Friday or Saturday as the \nridge will have move far enough west such that the \"ridge rider\" \nstorms may be able to work their way into west Texas on its \nperiphery.",
